      "metadata": {
        "id": "de9adb47"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section 2: Import e check GPU\n",
        "Importa TensorFlow/NumPy, controlla versione e disponibilità GPU."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 18,
      "id": "c0359585",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "c0359585",
        "outputId": "a92436f5-6c2f-4f5f-c153-6f3ed1a69853"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "TF 2.19.0\n",
            "GPU available: True\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import tensorflow as tf\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import h5py, os\n",
        "\n",
        "print('TF', tf.__version__)\n",
        "print('GPU available:', len(tf.config.list_physical_devices('GPU')) > 0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "e73f15a6",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e73f15a6"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section 3: Caricamento dataset HDF5\n",
        "Carica train/val da `dataset.h5` e unisce i due split per l'analisi."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 19,
      "id": "65d16edd",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "65d16edd",
        "outputId": "67335f61-da13-45d0-e989-d65f18ea9aad"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Shapes (26605, 128, 128, 3) (26605,)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "DATASET_PATH = '/content/drive/MyDrive/TESI_POLITO/dataset/dataset/dataset.h5'\n",
        "with h5py.File(DATASET_PATH, 'r') as f:\n",
        "    X_train = np.array(f['X_train'])\n",
        "    y_train = np.array(f['y_train'])\n",
        "    X_val = np.array(f['X_val'])\n",
        "    y_val = np.array(f['y_val'])\n",
        "    class_names = [c.decode('utf-8') for c in f['class_names']]\n",
        "X = np.concatenate([X_train, X_val])\n",
        "y = np.concatenate([y_train, y_val])\n",
        "print('Shapes', X.shape, y.shape)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "9d43aaa5",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9d43aaa5"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section 4: Individuazione classi rare\n",
        "Trova classi con frequenza <15% della classe più numerosa e visualizza la distribuzione."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 4,
      "id": "d200b507",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d200b507",
        "outputId": "0f8e3e08-7751-4745-eb54-5a8baacbfb12",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 613
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Rare classes: {np.int64(1): 'DISGUST', np.int64(6): 'SURPRISE'}\n",
            "ANGRY     : 3286\n",
            "DISGUST   : 642\n",
            "FEAR      : 2843\n",
            "HAPPY     : 13742\n",
            "NEUTRAL   : 2457\n",
            "SAD       : 2848\n",
            "SURPRISE  : 787\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "image/png": "",
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "counts = np.bincount(y)\n",
        "max_count = counts.max()\n",
        "rare_idx = np.where(counts < 0.15 * max_count)[0]\n",
        "rare_names = [class_names[i] for i in rare_idx]\n",
        "print('Rare classes:', dict(zip(rare_idx, rare_names)))\n",
        "for i, n in enumerate(class_names):\n",
        "    print(f'{n:10s}: {counts[i]}')\n",
        "plt.bar(class_names, counts)\n",
        "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "81d244d5",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "81d244d5"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section 5: Prepara subset classi rare\n",
        "Filtra solo le classi rare, normalizza in [-1,1], rimappa etichette a indice locale e applica one-hot."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "id": "c9774116",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c9774116",
        "outputId": "32ec75f2-4c94-4c1a-9cc3-87edf0b46742",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Rare subset (1429, 128, 128, 3) (1429, 2)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "mask = np.isin(y, rare_idx)\n",
        "X_rare = X[mask].astype('float32') / 127.5 - 1.0\n",
        "y_rare = y[mask]\n",
        "label_map = {old:new for new, old in enumerate(rare_idx)}\n",
        "y_remap = np.array([label_map[v] for v in y_rare])\n",
        "num_classes = len(rare_idx)\n",
        "y_onehot = tf.keras.utils.to_categorical(y_remap, num_classes)\n",
        "print('Rare subset', X_rare.shape, y_onehot.shape)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "e4fd28c9",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e4fd28c9"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section 6: Hyperparameter setup\n",
        "Definisci dimensione immagine, latente, batch, LR e parametri WGAN-GP (λ_GP, critic_steps)."
      ]
    },
